<</Type/StructElem/S/Diagram/Alt(Outputs are the final products, results, or services that a system delivers after processing inputs. \rTo keep output meaningful, data visualization tools transform raw numbers into charts and graphs to make outputs more comprehensible. \rOutputs can also take non-physical forms, such as automated alerts, notifications, or even machine actions. For example, a traffic control system may output a red-light signal to regulate vehicle flow. \rRegardless of form, the quality of outputs reflects the effectiveness of the entire system and determines user satisfaction.\r\(Icon Vertical Solid List\))/K[1 2 3 4]/A 432 0 R/P 430 0 R/Pg 30 0 R>>
