<</Type/StructElem/S/Diagram/Alt(Feedback is the information a system receives about its performance \(Output\), while control is the mechanism that uses this feedback to guide system behavior. \rTogether, they ensure that the system stays aligned with its objectives. For example, in a thermostat-controlled heating system, temperature sensors provide feedback, and the thermostat adjusts heating levels to maintain the desired temperature.\rFeedback can be positive or negative. Positive feedback reinforces and strengthens system behavior, while negative feedback signals problems that require corrective action. \r\(Staggered Process\))/K[1 2 3 4]/A 459 0 R/P 457 0 R/Pg 33 0 R>>
