465 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Diagram/Alt(By analyzing both, the system can adjust processes to improve performance. Control mechanisms establish rules and standards for how the system should respond to feedback. \rIn organizations, this could mean setting thresholds for performance indicators, such as maximum error rates or minimum response times. \rIf actual outputs deviate from these standards, corrective actions are triggered. For example, in manufacturing, feedback from quality checks ensures defective products are identified and adjustments are made to maintain standards.\r\(Staggered Process\))/K[1 2 3 4]/A 466 0 R/P 464 0 R/Pg 34 0 R>>
