<</Type/StructElem/S/Diagram/Alt(However, Informal systems, on the other hand, are not based on official documentation or strict rules. \rThey rely on personal interactions, relationships, trust, and shared understandings that emerge naturally within organizations or communities. \rFor example, when employees collaborate through casual discussions, social networks, or mentorship outside formal procedures, they are using an informal system. \rThese systems are highly flexible, adaptive, and often faster at solving unexpected problems compared to formal ones, making them crucial for innovation and quick decision-making.\r\(Icon Vertical Solid List\))/K[1 2 3 4]/A 539 0 R/P 537 0 R/Pg 41 0 R>>
